Attribution
-----------
Please credit:

  - HECTOR: Historical Economic Commodities: Terminologies, Ontologies, & Rates,
    https://w3id.org/hector/ (Stephen Gadd, docuracy);
  - Stuart Jenks, whose transcriptions of the Tudor Books of Rates and of the London
    customs accounts the records are derived from;
  - the London Customs Accounts project (IHR, AHRC/DFG "Unlocking Upcycled Medieval
    Data"), whose glossary supplies the commodities and units,
    https://w3id.org/mlca/.

Material from other sources keeps its own terms: identifiers and labels quoted from the
Getty Art & Architecture Thesaurus (ODC-By 1.0) and Wikidata (CC0), cited with each record.
No OpenStreetMap or OpenHistoricalMap data (ODbL) is included.

Status
------
ALPHA (since 3 Oct 2026): the data are published for discussion and are not yet for
citation. Records and URIs may change or be withdrawn until the first full release.

Decided 29 Sep 2026 (PLAN.md, decision D5): CC BY 4.0, the same licence as the London
Customs Accounts' own data. Stuart Jenks granted CC BY 4.0 on his transcriptions and on all
data derived from them, for HECTOR and the London Customs Accounts project and for anyone
reusing them, by signed letter received 3 October 2026 (PLAN.md, task 1).
